\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. God is a name my soul adores,
\par The almighty Three, the eternal One;
\par Nature and grace with all their powers,
\par Confess the infinite unknown.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Thy voice produced the sea and spheres,
\par ade the waves roar, the planets shine;
\par But nothing like Thyself appear 
\par Through all these spacious works of Thine
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Still restless nature dies and grows,
\par From change to change the creatures run;
\par Thy being no succession knows,
\par And all thy vast designs are one.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. A glance of Thine runs through the globe.
\par Rules the bright worlds, and moves their frame;
\par Of light Thou form'st Thy dazzling robe,
\par Thy ministers are living flame.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. How shall polluted mortals dare
\par To sing Thy glory or Thy grace?
\par Beneath Thy feet we lie afar,
\par And see but shadows of Thy face.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Who can behold the blazing light?
\par Who can approach consuming flame?
\par None but Thy wisdom knows Thy mighty,
\par None but Thy word can speak Thy name. 
\par \lang1033\f1 
\par \cf1\lang2057\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

